  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This CPO addresses long-standing challenges related to employers&#x2019; freedom of association, representativeness, and effective participation in social dialogue in Armenia. The expected results include strengthened institutional capacity of employers&#x2019; organizations to operate in line with the evolving legal framework, improved internal governance, expanded membership, and enhanced ability to engage in policy dialogue on labour and economic issues. Particular emphasis is placed on supporting employers&#x2019; organizations to implement governance reforms, develop membership strategies, and strengthen their policy and advocacy functions following recent organizational and legislative changes.
The primary beneficiaries are employers&#x2019; organizations and their member enterprises, including small and medium-sized businesses, which will benefit from stronger representation and more effective engagement with public institutions. The strategy is implemented in close cooperation with government institutions responsible for labour and social policy, workers&#x2019; organizations, and international partners, with the aim of restoring balanced and effective tripartite dialogue and contributing to a more enabling environment for enterprises and decent work.</narrative>
  </description>
